========================================================================================
(A) r(M,N), DECISIVE (ascending-r, one big S, two primes, >=20 holdout)
========================================================================================
  (M,N)=(1,1)  D=2  ->  r = 2             [C(D,M)=2, D=2, D-[M==N]=1]
  (M,N)=(1,2)  D=3  ->  r = DISAGREE [2, 3]  [C(D,M)=3, D=3, D-[M==N]=3]
  (M,N)=(1,3)  D=4  ->  r = 4             [C(D,M)=4, D=4, D-[M==N]=4]
  (M,N)=(2,2)  D=4  ->  r = 4             [C(D,M)=6, D=4, D-[M==N]=3]
  (M,N)=(1,4)  D=5  ->  r = 5             [C(D,M)=5, D=5, D-[M==N]=5]
  (M,N)=(2,3)  D=5  ->  r = 5             [C(D,M)=10, D=5, D-[M==N]=5]
  (M,N)=(1,5)  D=6  ->  r = 6             [C(D,M)=6, D=6, D-[M==N]=6]
  (M,N)=(2,4)  D=6  ->  r = 6             [C(D,M)=15, D=6, D-[M==N]=6]
  (M,N)=(3,3)  D=6  ->  r = 6             [C(D,M)=20, D=6, D-[M==N]=5]

  r(M,N) summary:  (order 2 <=> orthogonal family)
     (1,1) D=2 : r=2
     (1,2) D=3 : r=DISAGREE [2, 3]
     (1,3) D=4 : r=4
     (1,4) D=5 : r=5
     (1,5) D=6 : r=6
     (2,2) D=4 : r=4
     (2,3) D=5 : r=5
     (2,4) D=6 : r=6
     (3,3) D=6 : r=6

========================================================================================
(B) DOES {disc(R)=0} FORCE P_0(0)=0?  normalisation-independent zero-test
========================================================================================

  (M,N)=(1,1) D=2 order r=2 coeff-deg s=1
     generic R (disc!=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  [False, False]   -> so P_0(0)!=0 off the disc locus: True
     double-root R (disc=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  []
     -> {disc=0} forces P_0(0)=0 (discriminant story holds here): True
  (1,2): order unresolved, skipping

  (M,N)=(2,2) D=4 order r=4 coeff-deg s=2
     generic R (disc!=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  [None, None, None]   -> so P_0(0)!=0 off the disc locus: False
     double-root R (disc=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  []
     -> {disc=0} forces P_0(0)=0 (discriminant story holds here): True

  (M,N)=(1,3) D=4 order r=4 coeff-deg s=6
     generic R (disc!=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  [False, False]   -> so P_0(0)!=0 off the disc locus: True
     double-root R (disc=0): P_0(0)==0 ?  []
     -> {disc=0} forces P_0(0)=0 (discriminant story holds here): True
